<title>UKRAINE: TABLE-Ukraine 6-mo T-bill yields down.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Ukraine 6-mo T-bill yields down.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average yields at auctions of six-month treasury bills eased to 20.05 percent from 20.13 percent at the last sales, a central bank statement said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The results of the six-month discount T-bill auction, compared to the last issue, were as follows:</p>
<p> Auction Number	   316		    307</p>
<p> Issue date		 July 30, 1997	July 24, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date	    January 28, 1998   January 23, 1998</p>
<p> Denominations	    100 hryvnia	  100 hryvnia</p>
<p> Issue volume	     no limit stated    22.00 million UAH</p>
<p> Amount sold		136.18 million UAH 6.29 million UAH</p>
<p> Actual amount raised   123.80 million UAH 5.72 million UAH</p>
<p> Average yield	    20.05 percent	20.13 percent</p>
<p> Average price	    90.91 hryvnia	90.88 hryvnia</p>
<p> Cut-off price	    90.91 hryvnia	90.88 hryvnia</p>
<p>The central bank sold 1,361,837 T-bills, the bank's statement said.</p>
<p>The next auction of six-month discount T-bills is scheduled for July 31.</p>
<p>--Kiev Newsroom +380 44 244-9150</p>
</text>
